---
import Md from '../components/typography/Markdown.astro'

import Main from '../layouts/Main.astro'
import Link from '../components/Link.astro'

const pageMeta = {
  title: 'About Me',
  description: "Full stack developer. Mentor. Loves tinkering all things tech.",
}

const markdownContent = `
# About Me

Hi, it's me, Andreas... or just call me Eas.

I love coding, tinkering, and solving each problems I found.

It started when I was 4, and at that time, I made my parent's computer unusable.
Since then, I wanted to learn more about computers, and I started to love it.

When I was 14, a family relative of mine lent me
[this book](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/3402859-joomla-website-magic)
of how to manage CMS sites using Joomla! CMS. With that book,
I started to learn how websites work.

But it was so hard due to the Internet connection was so expensive and scarce
at that time. So I decided to borrow his computer, and try some plugins
mentioned on the book... in exchange of doing his favor: packing soy milk
(it was delicious, by the way).

Years later, I started to learn PHP as my first programming language to learn
more about how websites (and later, web apps) work. Now, I'm starting to create
solutions for real-life problems by developing sites, apps, and platforms,
starting with the small ones. You can find all of these within
[my portfolios page](/portfolios).

I also currently work as a full-time teacher at [Hacktiv8](https://hacktiv8.com),
sharing all of what I've learned so far about JavaScript. But if there's something
that I found outside of my teaching job, I'll share it here -- I'll try to be
as concise as possible.

If you want to reach out to me, [feel free to contact me](/contact). I'll be
happy to reply you back!
`

---

<Main meta={ pageMeta }>
  <article>
    <Link text="Go Back" to="/" size="" type="" />

    <div class="section__content">
      <Md content={ markdownContent } />
    </div>
  </article>
</Main>
